Installing the Kernel and System Modules

1. Create the boot directory in your target environment:

`mkdir -p /boot`

2. Copy the Gentoo binary kernel and initramfs images from the host system into /boot:

`cp -av /boot/vmlinuz* $KLFS/boot/`
`cp -av /boot/initramfs* $KLFS/boot/`

3. Copy the compiled kernel modules to match your kernel version:

`cp -av /lib/modules/* $KLFS/lib/modules/`

4. Verify that the kernel image and kernel module directories are in place:

`ls -lh /boot`
`ls -lh /lib/modules`
